<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--
CajunLyrics Lyrics API
https://www.cajunlyrics.com/?page=api
No user ID or token required

See also: https://www.programmableweb.com/api/cajunlyrics-rest-api
-->
<configuration>

    <configSections>
        <section name="lyricService" type="System.Configuration.IgnoreSectionHandler, System.Configuration, Version=4.0.0.0, Culture=neutral, PublicKeyToken=b03f5f7f11d50a3a" />
    </configSections>

    <!-- 
    The lyricService settings are only used during the first/initial startup.
    After the first/initial startup, the XML datafile is used for keeping the settings.
    The XML datafile location is defined in the "LyricsFinderCore.dll.config" configuration file, 
    in the "localAppDataFile" appSetting.
    Default XML datafile location:
    "%USERPROFILE%\Documents\LyricsFinder\LyricsFinder.xml" 

    This service uses the element form: every setting is a child element of "lyricService", and a
    line break written literally inside the element content survives. The parser normalises CR+LF
    to a single LF (XML 1.0, section 2.11) and the reader turns it back into CR+LF.

    WARNING: the continuation lines of a multi line value MUST start in column 1, because their
    indentation would otherwise become part of the value.

    The alternative is the attribute form, where a line break written literally inside an attribute
    value is replaced by a single space when the file is read (XML 1.0, section 3.3.3), so the
    &#xD;&#xA; character references have to be used instead. Both forms are read, and both may
    appear in the same file; on a clash the element form wins.

    The lyricService section is declared in configSections with IgnoreSectionHandler purely so
    that System.Configuration does not reject the file as having an unrecognized section. The
    settings themselves are read straight from the XML by AbstractLyricService.ReadServiceSettings,
    so the handler is never invoked.
    -->
    <lyricService>
        <Company>CajunLyrics</Company>
        <CreditUrl>https://www.cajunlyrics.com</CreditUrl>
        <DateFormat>yyyy.MM.dd</DateFormat>
        <ServiceName>CajunLyrics</ServiceName>
        <ServiceUrl>http://api.cajunlyrics.com</ServiceUrl>

        <Comment>No user ID or token required.</Comment>

        <CreditTextFormat>

-----------------------------------------------------------
Found by LyricsFinder for JRiver MediaCenter on {Date}
Lyrics found in {ServiceName}
{Company} - {CreditUrl}
{ServiceName} - {ServiceUrl}
-----------------------------------------------------------
</CreditTextFormat>
    </lyricService>

    <startup>
        <supportedRuntime version="v4.0" sku=".NETFramework,Version=v4.8" />
    </startup>

